libpkgreconcile-apply-posix(3)

# NAME

libpkgreconcile-apply-posix - verify rejected evidence before durable \
reconciliation publication

# DESCRIPTION

*libpkgreconcile-apply-posix* composes a completed *libpkgreconcile-apply*
projection with an explicitly routed *libpkgapply-posix* rejected-object store
and a target-bound *libpkgreconcile-posix* inventory store.

*publish_verified_projection()* reopens every projected rejected record by its
exact record identity and verifies the routed store identity, object identity,
operation-plan identity, physical application-attempt identity, package path,
and concrete source side. Reopened provider handles are released per tuple so
verification descriptor use remains bounded independently of batch size. Only
after every tuple is verified is the complete pending batch offered to the
reconciliation store.

# ROUTING

The caller supplies the exact *rejected_object_store_identity* already resolved
to the authorized rejected-store handle. The library does not derive that
identity from a pathname or descriptor and does not scan provider-private store
layout.

The rejected-object locator is decoded through the public
*libpkgreconcile-apply* decoder rather than interpreted locally.

# FAILURE

Semantic composition refusals are reported as *publication_error*. Concrete
rejected-store and reconciliation-store mechanism failures remain their
providers' errors and propagate unchanged.

# BOUNDARY

The library does not plan application work, mutate the target, discover rejected
stores, persist reconciliation formats itself, choose reconciliation
dispositions, or coordinate transaction restart/publication ordering.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgreconcile-apply*(3),
*libpkgapply-posix*(3),
*libpkgreconcile-posix*(3)
